From 57e1e0836c9bf20bb4793801890980021e2c556a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Enver Ikromov <owner@ph4ntom-rev.uz>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 19:50:19 +0500
Subject: [PATCH v4 4/4] wifi: rtw89: restore channel after monitor restart on
 non-chanctx chips

Wi-Fi 6 rtw89 chips (such as RTL8852A, RTL8852B, and RTL8851B) have
support_chanctx_num == 0 and rely on mac80211 chanctx emulation via
hw->conf.chandef and rtw89_ops_config().

When the last monitor interface is brought down or deleted,
rtw89_ops_stop() powers down the MAC/BB/RF and clears the
RTW89_PHY_0 entity state, while mac80211 retains the previous
local->hw.conf.chandef. When a monitor interface is brought up
again on the same channel, ieee80211_hw_conf_chan() sees no
chandef change and omits IEEE80211_CONF_CHANGE_CHANNEL, leaving
the RF uncalibrated and RX/TX silent until the user manually
switches to a different channel and back.

In rtw89_ops_config(), when IEEE80211_CONF_CHANGE_MONITOR enables
IEEE80211_CONF_MONITOR on non-chanctx chips and RTW89_PHY_0 is not
yet active, apply hw->conf.chandef and call rtw89_set_channel().
On initial bringup where IEEE80211_CONF_CHANGE_CHANNEL has already
configured RTW89_PHY_0, the entity state check is already true and
avoids redundant RF calibration.

Signed-off-by: Enver Ikromov <owner@ph4ntom-rev.uz>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw89/mac80211.c | 12 +++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw89/mac80211.c b/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw89/mac80211.c
index dc03b26..c06bdd9 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw89/mac80211.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw89/mac80211.c
@@ -118,9 +118,19 @@ static int rtw89_ops_config(struct ieee80211_hw *hw, int radio_idx, u32 changed)
 	    !rtwdev->scanning)
 		rtw89_enter_ips(rtwdev);
 
-	if (changed & IEEE80211_CONF_CHANGE_MONITOR)
+	if (changed & IEEE80211_CONF_CHANGE_MONITOR) {
 		rtw89_physts_parsing_init(rtwdev);
 
+		if ((hw->conf.flags & IEEE80211_CONF_MONITOR) &&
+		    !rtwdev->chip->support_chanctx_num &&
+		    !rtw89_get_entity_state(rtwdev, RTW89_PHY_0) &&
+		    cfg80211_chandef_valid(&hw->conf.chandef)) {
+			rtw89_config_entity_chandef(rtwdev, RTW89_CHANCTX_0,
+						    &hw->conf.chandef);
+			rtw89_set_channel(rtwdev);
+		}
+	}
+
 	return 0;
 }
 
